# Module: broadcast
Compile unit for the Forum Frontend.
Generates: `frontend/src/components/broadcast.tsx` (current hand-authored code is the reference output)

## Behavior
- Chyron-style LIVE ticker at the top of the page: blinking live dot, "AI CREATOR BROADCAST" label, one rotating message at a time (slide-in), mono typeface from the frozen `styles.css` tokens.
- Hydrates from `GET /api/broadcast` and appends live `broadcast_events` INSERTs via Supabase Realtime (mock mode cycles a scripted playlist).
- Renders orchestrator micro-copy verbatim — friendly agent narration only, never raw logs or build output (that filtering is upstream; this component just displays).
- **Two ticker sources, kept distinct**: pipeline phase events (`screening|synthesizing|architecting|compiling|deployed`) come from the `broadcast_events` feed above and are rendered verbatim. Any community-engagement / ambient copy ("27 members are VOTING", "on a hype streak") is **client-computed flavor** from data the app already holds — interleave it locally if desired, but it is never part of the `broadcast_events` feed and is never sent back to the backend.
- `deployed`-phase events style in the success (mint) accent. `role="status"` / `aria-live="polite"` for accessibility.

